('storm_giant','Storm Giant','Storm Giant','13','Huge','Giant','Often chaotic good','19d8+114 (199 hp)',199,'+2','35 ft. (7 squares), swim 30 ft. (6 squares) in breastplate; base speed 50 ft., swim 40 ft.','27 (–2 size, +2 Dex, +12 natural, +5 breastplate) touch 10, flat-footed 25','+14/+36','Greatsword +26 melee (4d6+21/19–20) or slam +26 melee (1d6+14) or composite longbow (+14 Str bonus) +14 ranged (3d6+14/x3)','15 ft./15 ft.','+17','+8','+13',39,14,23,16,20,15,'Climb +20, Concentration +26, Craft (any one) +13, Diplomacy +4, Intimidate +12, Jump +24, Listen +15, Perform (sing) +12, Sense Motive +15, Spot +25, Swim +18*','Awesome Blow, Cleave, Combat Reflexes, Improved Bull Rush, Improved Sunder, Iron Will, Power Attack','{"special_attacks":"Spell-like abilities","special_qualities":"Freedom of movement, immunity to electricity, low-light vision, rock catching, water breathing"}'::jsonb,'Very rarely, storm giants have violet skin. Violet-skinned storm giants have deep violet or blue-black hair with silvery gray or purple eyes. Adults are about 21 feet tall and weigh about 12,000 pounds. Storm giants can live to be 600 years old. Storm giants’ garb is usually a short, loose tunic belted at the waist, sandals or bare feet, and a headband. They wear a few pieces of simple but finely crafted jewelry, anklets (favored by barefoot giants), rings, or circlets being most common. They live quiet, reflective lives and spend their time musing about the world, composing and playing music, and tilling their land or gathering food.','{"full_attack":"Greatsword +26/+21/+16 melee (4d6+21/19–20) or 2 slams +26 melee (1d6+14) or composite longbow (+14 Str bonus) +14/+9/+4 ranged (3d6+14/x3)","statblock":{"hit_dice":"19d8+114 (199 hp)","hit_points":199,"base_attack_grapple":"+14/+36","attack":"Greatsword +26 melee (4d6+21/19–20) or slam +26 melee (1d6+14) or composite longbow (+14 Str bonus) +14 ranged (3d6+14/x3)","full_attack":"Greatsword +26/+21/+16 melee (4d6+21/19–20) or 2 slams +26 melee (1d6+14) or composite longbow (+14 Str bonus) +14/+9/+4 ranged (3d6+14/x3)","space_reach":"15 ft./15 ft.","saves":"Fort +17, Ref +8, Will +13","abilities":{"str":"39","dex":"14","con":"23","int":"16","wis":"20","cha":"15"},"skills":"Climb +20, Concentration +26, Craft (any one) +13, Diplomacy +4, Intimidate +12, Jump +24, Listen +15, Perform (sing) +12, Sense Motive +15, Spot +25, Swim +18*","feats":"Awesome Blow, Cleave, Combat Reflexes, Improved Bull Rush, Improved Sunder, Iron Will, Power Attack","special_attacks":"Spell-like abilities","special_qualities":"Freedom of movement, immunity to electricity, low-light vision, rock catching, water breathing"},"source_file":"monsters-g.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-g.html',true),
('gibbering_mouther','Gibbering Mouther','Gibbering Mouther','5','Medium','Aberration','Usually neutral','4d8+24 (42 hp)',42,'+1','10 ft. (2 squares), swim 20 ft.','19 (+1 Dex, +8 natural), touch 11, flat-footed 18','+3/+3','Bite +4 melee (1) or spittle +4 ranged touch (1d4 acid plus blindness)','5 ft./5 ft.','+7','+4','+5',10,13,22,4,13,13,'Listen +4, Spot +9, Swim +8','Lightning Reflexes, Weapon Finesse','{"special_attacks":"Gibbering, spittle, improved grab, blood drain, engulf, ground manipulation","special_qualities":"Amorphous, damage reduction 5/bludgeoning, darkvision 60 ft."}'::jsonb,'A gibbering mouther is a horrible creature seemingly drawn from a lunatic’s nightmares. Although not evil, it thirsts after bodily fluids and seems to prefer the blood of intelligent creatures.

A gibbering mouther is about 3 feet across and 3 to 4 feet high. It weighs about 200 pounds.

Gibbering mouthers can speak Common, but seldom say anything other than gibberish.','{"full_attack":"6 bites +4 melee (1) and spittle +4 ranged touch (1d4 acid plus blindness)","statblock":{"hit_dice":"4d8+24 (42 hp)","hit_points":42,"base_attack_grapple":"+3/+3","attack":"Bite +4 melee (1) or spittle +4 ranged touch (1d4 acid plus blindness)","full_attack":"6 bites +4 melee (1) and spittle +4 ranged touch (1d4 acid plus blindness)","space_reach":"5 ft./5 ft.","saves":"Fort +7, Ref +4, Will +5","abilities":{"str":"10","dex":"13","con":"22","int":"4","wis":"13","cha":"13"},"skills":"Listen +4, Spot +9, Swim +8","feats":"Lightning Reflexes, Weapon Finesse","special_attacks":"Gibbering, spittle, improved grab, blood drain, engulf, ground manipulation","special_qualities":"Amorphous, damage reduction 5/bludgeoning, darkvision 60 ft."},"source_file":"monsters-g.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-g.html',true),
('girallon','Girallon','Girallon','6','Large','Magical Beast','Always neutral','7d10+20 (58 hp)',58,'+3','40 ft. (8 squares), climb 40 ft.','16 (–1 size, +3 Dex, +4 natural), touch 12, flat-footed 15','+7/+17','Claw +12 melee (1d4+6)','10 ft./10 ft.','+7','+8','+5',22,17,14,2,12,7,'Climb +14, Move Silently +8, Spot +6','Iron Will, Toughness (2)','{"special_attacks":"Rend 2d4+9","special_qualities":"Darkvision 60 ft., low-light vision, scent"}'::jsonb,'Girallons are savage, magical cousins of the gorilla. When moving on the ground, a girallon walks on its legs and lower arms. An adult girallon is about 8 feet tall, broad-chested, and covered in thick, pure white fur. It weighs about 800 pounds.','{"full_attack":"4 claws +12 melee (1d4+6) and bite +7 melee (1d8+3)","statblock":{"hit_dice":"7d10+20 (58 hp)","hit_points":58,"base_attack_grapple":"+7/+17","attack":"Claw +12 melee (1d4+6)","full_attack":"4 claws +12 melee (1d4+6) and bite +7 melee (1d8+3)","space_reach":"10 ft./10 ft.","saves":"Fort +7, Ref +8, Will +5","abilities":{"str":"22","dex":"17","con":"14","int":"2","wis":"12","cha":"7"},"skills":"Climb +14, Move Silently +8, Spot +6","feats":"Iron Will, Toughness (2)","special_attacks":"Rend 2d4+9","special_qualities":"Darkvision 60 ft., low-light vision, scent"},"source_file":"monsters-g.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-g.html',true),
('gnoll','Gnoll','Gnoll','1','Medium','Humanoid (Gnoll)','Usually chaotic evil','2d8+2 (11 hp)',11,'+0','30 ft. (6 squares)','15 (+1 natural, +2 leather armor, +2 heavy steel shield), touch 10, flat-footed 15','+1/+3','Battleaxe +3 melee (1d8+2/x3) or shortbow +1 ranged (1d6/x3)','5 ft./5 ft.','+4','+0','+0',15,10,13,8,11,8,'Listen +2, Spot +3','Power Attack','{"special_attacks":"—","special_qualities":"Darkvision 60 ft."}'::jsonb,'Gnolls are hyena-headed, evil humanoids that wander in loose tribes. Most gnolls have dirty yellow or reddish-brown fur. A gnoll is a nocturnal carnivore, preferring intelligent creatures for food because they scream more. A gnoll is about 7-1/2 feet tall and weighs 300 pounds. Gnolls speak Gnoll.','{"full_attack":"Battleaxe +3 melee (1d8+2/x3) or shortbow +1 ranged (1d6/x3)","statblock":{"hit_dice":"2d8+2 (11 hp)","hit_points":11,"base_attack_grapple":"+1/+3","attack":"Battleaxe +3 melee (1d8+2/x3) or shortbow +1 ranged (1d6/x3)","full_attack":"Battleaxe +3 melee (1d8+2/x3) or shortbow +1 ranged (1d6/x3)","space_reach":"5 ft./5 ft.","saves":"Fort +4, Ref +0, Will +0","abilities":{"str":"15","dex":"10","con":"13","int":"8","wis":"11","cha":"8"},"skills":"Listen +2, Spot +3","feats":"Power Attack","special_attacks":"—","special_qualities":"Darkvision 60 ft."},"source_file":"monsters-g.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-g.html',true),
('gnome_1st_level_warrior','Gnome, 1st-Level Warrior','Gnome, 1st-Level Warrior','1/2','Small','Humanoid (Gnome)','Usually neutral good','1d8+2 (6 hp)',6,'+0','20 ft. (4 squares)','16 (+1 size, +4 chain shirt, +1 light shield), touch 11, flat-footed 16','+1/–3','Longsword +2 melee (1d6/19–20) or light crossbow +3 ranged (1d6/19–20)','5 ft./5 ft.','+4','+0','–1',11,11,14,10,9,8,'Hide +3, Listen +1, Spot +1','Weapon Focus (light crossbow)','{"special_attacks":"—","special_qualities":"Gnome traits"}'::jsonb,'Gnomes stand 3 to 3-1/2 feet tall and weigh 40 to 45 pounds. Their skin color ranges from dark tan to woody brown, their hair is fair, and their eyes can be any shade of blue. Gnome males prefer short, carefully trimmed beards. Gnomes generally wear leather or earth tones, though they decorate their clothes with intricate stitching or fine jewelry. Gnomes reach adulthood at about age 40, and they live about 350 years, though some can live almost 500 years.

Gnomes speak their own language, Gnome. Most gnomes who travel outside gnome lands (as traders, tinkers, or adventurers) know Common, while warriors in gnome settlements usually learn Goblin.

Most gnomes encountered outside their home are warriors; the information in the statistics block is for one of 1st level.','{"full_attack":"Longsword +2 melee (1d6/19–20) or light crossbow +3 ranged (1d6/19–20)","statblock":{"hit_dice":"1d8+2 (6 hp)","hit_points":6,"base_attack_grapple":"+1/–3","attack":"Longsword +2 melee (1d6/19–20) or light crossbow +3 ranged (1d6/19–20)","full_attack":"Longsword +2 melee (1d6/19–20) or light crossbow +3 ranged (1d6/19–20)","space_reach":"5 ft./5 ft.","saves":"Fort +4, Ref +0, Will –1","abilities":{"str":"11","dex":"11","con":"14","int":"10","wis":"9","cha":"8"},"skills":"Hide +3, Listen +1, Spot +1","feats":"Weapon Focus (light crossbow)","special_attacks":"—","special_qualities":"Gnome traits"},"source_file":"monsters-g.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-g.html',true),
('svirfneblin_1st_level_warrior','Svirfneblin, 1st-Level Warrior','Svirfneblin, 1st-Level Warrior','1','Small','Humanoid (Gnome)','Usually neutral','1d8+4 (8 hp)',8,'+1','15 ft. in banded mail armor (3 squares); base speed 20 ft.','23 (+1 size, +1 Dex, +4 dodge, +6 banded mail, +1 buckler), touch 16, flat-footed 18','+1/–3','Heavy pick +2 melee (1d4/x4) or light crossbow +3 ranged (1d6/19–20)','5 ft./5 ft.','+5','+3','+2',11,13,12,10,11,4,'Hide +2, Listen +2, Spot +2','Toughness','{"special_attacks":"Spell-like abilities","special_qualities":"Gnome traits, svirfneblin traits, spell resistance 12"}'::jsonb,'Gnomes stand 3 to 3-1/2 feet tall and weigh 40 to 45 pounds. Their skin color ranges from dark tan to woody brown, their hair is fair, and their eyes can be any shade of blue. Gnome males prefer short, carefully trimmed beards. Gnomes generally wear leather or earth tones, though they decorate their clothes with intricate stitching or fine jewelry. Gnomes reach adulthood at about age 40, and they live about 350 years, though some can live almost 500 years.

Gnomes speak their own language, Gnome. Most gnomes who travel outside gnome lands (as traders, tinkers, or adventurers) know Common, while warriors in gnome settlements usually learn Goblin.

Most gnomes encountered outside their home are warriors; the information in the statistics block is for one of 1st level.','{"full_attack":"Heavy pick +2 melee (1d4/x4) or light crossbow +3 ranged (1d6/19–20)","statblock":{"hit_dice":"1d8+4 (8 hp)","hit_points":8,"base_attack_grapple":"+1/–3","attack":"Heavy pick +2 melee (1d4/x4) or light crossbow +3 ranged (1d6/19–20)","full_attack":"Heavy pick +2 melee (1d4/x4) or light crossbow +3 ranged (1d6/19–20)","space_reach":"5 ft./5 ft.","saves":"Fort +5, Ref +3, Will +2","abilities":{"str":"11","dex":"13","con":"12","int":"10","wis":"11","cha":"4"},"skills":"Hide +2, Listen +2, Spot +2","feats":"Toughness","special_attacks":"Spell-like abilities","special_qualities":"Gnome traits, svirfneblin traits, spell resistance 12"},"source_file":"monsters-g.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-g.html',true),
('goblin','Goblin','Goblin, 1st-Level Warrior','1/3','Small','Humanoid (Goblinoid)','Usually neutral evil','1d8+1 (5 hp)',5,'+1','30 ft. (6 squares)','15 (+1 size, +1 Dex, +2 leather armor, +1 light shield), touch 12, flat-footed 14','+1/–3','Morningstar +2 melee (1d6) or javelin +3 ranged (1d4)','5 ft./5 ft.','+3','+1','–1',11,13,12,10,9,6,'Hide +5, Listen +2, Move Silently +5, Ride +4, Spot +2','Alertness','{"special_attacks":"—","special_qualities":"Darkvision 60 ft."}'::jsonb,'A goblin stands 3 to 3-1/2 feet tall and weigh 40 to 45 pounds. Its eyes are usually dull and glazed, varying in color from red to yellow. A goblin’s skin color ranges from yellow through any shade of orange to a deep red; usually all members of a single tribe are about the same color. Goblins wear clothing of dark leather, tending toward drab, soiled-looking colors. Goblins speak Goblin; those with Intelligence scores of 12 or higher also speak Common.

Most goblins encountered outside their homes are warriors; the information in the statistics block is for one of 1st level.','{"full_attack":"Morningstar +2 melee (1d6) or javelin +3 ranged (1d4)","statblock":{"hit_dice":"1d8+1 (5 hp)","hit_points":5,"base_attack_grapple":"+1/–3","attack":"Morningstar +2 melee (1d6) or javelin +3 ranged (1d4)","full_attack":"Morningstar +2 melee (1d6) or javelin +3 ranged (1d4)","space_reach":"5 ft./5 ft.","saves":"Fort +3, Ref +1, Will –1","abilities":{"str":"11","dex":"13","con":"12","int":"10","wis":"9","cha":"6"},"skills":"Hide +5, Listen +2, Move Silently +5, Ride +4, Spot +2","feats":"Alertness","special_attacks":"—","special_qualities":"Darkvision 60 ft."},"source_file":"monsters-g.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-g.html',true),
('clay_golem','Clay Golem','Clay Golem','10','Large','Construct','Always neutral','11d10+30 (90 hp)',90,'–1','20 ft. (4 squares)','22 (–1 size, –1 Dex, +14 natural), touch 8, flat-footed 22','+8/+19','Slam +14 melee (2d10+7 plus cursed wound)','10 ft./10 ft.','+3','+2','+3',25,9,null,null,11,1,'—','—','{"special_attacks":"Berserk, cursed wound","special_qualities":"Construct traits, damage reduction 10/adamantine and bludgeoning, darkvision 60 ft., haste, immunity to magic, low-light vision"}'::jsonb,'This golem has a humanoid body made from clay. A clay golem wears no clothing except for a metal or stiff leather garment around its hips.

A clay golem golem cannot speak or make any vocal noise. It walks and moves with a slow, clumsy gait. It weighs around 600 pounds.','{"full_attack":"2 slams +14 melee (2d10+7 plus cursed wound)","statblock":{"hit_dice":"11d10+30 (90 hp)","hit_points":90,"base_attack_grapple":"+8/+19","attack":"Slam +14 melee (2d10+7 plus cursed wound)","full_attack":"2 slams +14 melee (2d10+7 plus cursed wound)","space_reach":"10 ft./10 ft.","saves":"Fort +3, Ref +2, Will +3","abilities":{"str":"25","dex":"9","con":null,"int":null,"wis":"11","cha":"1"},"skills":"—","feats":"—","special_attacks":"Berserk, cursed wound","special_qualities":"Construct traits, damage reduction 10/adamantine and bludgeoning, darkvision 60 ft., haste, immunity to magic, low-light vision"},"source_file":"monsters-g.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-g.html',true),
('flesh_golem','Flesh Golem','Flesh Golem','7','Large','Construct','Always neutral','9d10+30 (79 hp)',79,'–1','30 ft. (6 squares)','18 (–1 size, –1 Dex, +10 natural), touch 8, flat-footed 18','+6/+15','Slam +10 melee (2d8+5)','10 ft./10 ft.','+3','+2','+3',21,9,null,null,11,1,'—','—','{"special_attacks":"Berserk","special_qualities":"Construct traits, damage reduction 5/adamantine, darkvision 60 ft., immunity to magic, low-light vision"}'::jsonb,'A flesh golem is a ghoulish collection of stolen humanoid body parts, stitched together into a single composite form. No natural animal willingly tracks a flesh golem. The golem wears whatever clothing its creator desires, usually just a ragged pair of trousers. It has no possessions and no weapons. It stands 8 feet tall and weighs almost 500 pounds.

A flesh golem golem cannot speak, although it can emit a hoarse roar of sorts. It walks and moves with a stiff-jointed gait, as if not in complete control of its body.','{"full_attack":"2 slams +10 melee (2d8+5)","statblock":{"hit_dice":"9d10+30 (79 hp)","hit_points":79,"base_attack_grapple":"+6/+15","attack":"Slam +10 melee (2d8+5)","full_attack":"2 slams +10 melee (2d8+5)","space_reach":"10 ft./10 ft.","saves":"Fort +3, Ref +2, Will +3","abilities":{"str":"21","dex":"9","con":null,"int":null,"wis":"11","cha":"1"},"skills":"—","feats":"—","special_attacks":"Berserk","special_qualities":"Construct traits, damage reduction 5/adamantine, darkvision 60 ft., immunity to magic, low-light vision"},"source_file":"monsters-g.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-g.html',true),
('iron_golem','Iron Golem','Iron Golem','13','Large','Construct','Always neutral','18d10+30 (129 hp)',129,'–1','20 ft. (4 squares)','30 (–1 size, –1 Dex, +22 natural) touch 8, flat-footed 30','+12/+28','Slam +23 melee (2d10+11)','10 ft./10 ft.','+6','+5','+6',33,9,null,null,11,1,'—','—','{"special_attacks":"Breath weapon","special_qualities":"Construct traits, damage reduction 15/adamantine, darkvision 60 ft., immunity to magic, low-light vision"}'::jsonb,'This golem has a humanoid body made from iron. An iron golem can be fashioned in any manner, just like a stone golem (see below), although it almost always displays armor of some sort. Its features are much smoother than those of a stone golem. Iron golems sometimes carry a short sword in one hand. An iron golem is 12 feet tall and weighs about 5,000 pounds. An iron golem cannot speak or make any vocal noise, nor does it have any distinguishable odor. It moves with a ponderous but smooth gait. Each step causes the floor to tremble unless it is on a thick, solid foundation.','{"full_attack":"2 slams +23 melee (2d10+11)","statblock":{"hit_dice":"18d10+30 (129 hp)","hit_points":129,"base_attack_grapple":"+12/+28","attack":"Slam +23 melee (2d10+11)","full_attack":"2 slams +23 melee (2d10+11)","space_reach":"10 ft./10 ft.","saves":"Fort +6, Ref +5, Will +6","abilities":{"str":"33","dex":"9","con":null,"int":null,"wis":"11","cha":"1"},"skills":"—","feats":"—","special_attacks":"Breath weapon","special_qualities":"Construct traits, damage reduction 15/adamantine, darkvision 60 ft., immunity to magic, low-light vision"},"source_file":"monsters-g.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-g.html',true),
('stone_golem','Stone Golem','Stone Golem','11','Large','Construct','Always neutral','14d10+30 (107 hp)',107,'–1','20 ft. (4 squares)','26 (–1 size, –1 Dex, +18 natural), touch 8, flat-footed 26','+10/+23','Slam +18 melee (2d10+9)','10 ft./10 ft.','+4','+3','+4',29,9,null,null,11,1,'—','—','{"special_attacks":"Slow","special_qualities":"Construct traits, damage reduction 10/adamantine, darkvision 60 ft., immunity to magic, low-light vision"}'::jsonb,'This golem has a humanoid body made from stone. A stone golem is 9 feet tall and weighs around 2,000 pounds. Its body is frequently stylized to suit its creator. For example, it might look like it is wearing armor, with a particular symbol carved on the breastplate, or have designs worked into the stone of its limbs.','{"full_attack":"2 slams +18 melee (2d10+9)","statblock":{"hit_dice":"14d10+30 (107 hp)","hit_points":107,"base_attack_grapple":"+10/+23","attack":"Slam +18 melee (2d10+9)","full_attack":"2 slams +18 melee (2d10+9)","space_reach":"10 ft./10 ft.","saves":"Fort +4, Ref +3, Will +4","abilities":{"str":"29","dex":"9","con":null,"int":null,"wis":"11","cha":"1"},"skills":"—","feats":"—","special_attacks":"Slow","special_qualities":"Construct traits, damage reduction 10/adamantine, darkvision 60 ft., immunity to magic, low-light vision"},"source_file":"monsters-g.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-g.html',true),
('greater_stone_golem','Greater Stone Golem','Greater Stone Golem','16','Huge','Construct','Always neutral','42d10+40 (271 hp)',271,'–2','20 ft. (4 squares)','27 (–2 size, –2 Dex, +21 natural), touch 6, flat-footed 27','+31/+52','Slam +42 melee (4d8+13)','15 ft./15 ft.','+14','+12','+14',37,7,null,null,11,1,'—','—','{"special_attacks":"Slow","special_qualities":"Construct traits, damage reduction 10/adamantine, darkvision 60 ft., immunity to magic, low-light vision"}'::jsonb,'This golem has a humanoid body made from stone. A stone golem is 9 feet tall and weighs around 2,000 pounds. Its body is frequently stylized to suit its creator. For example, it might look like it is wearing armor, with a particular symbol carved on the breastplate, or have designs worked into the stone of its limbs.','{"full_attack":"2 slams +42 melee (4d8+13)","statblock":{"hit_dice":"42d10+40 (271 hp)","hit_points":271,"base_attack_grapple":"+31/+52","attack":"Slam +42 melee (4d8+13)","full_attack":"2 slams +42 melee (4d8+13)","space_reach":"15 ft./15 ft.","saves":"Fort +14, Ref +12, Will +14","abilities":{"str":"37","dex":"7","con":null,"int":null,"wis":"11","cha":"1"},"skills":"—","feats":"—","special_attacks":"Slow","special_qualities":"Construct traits, damage reduction 10/adamantine, darkvision 60 ft., immunity to magic, low-light vision"},"source_file":"monsters-g.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-g.html',true),
('gorgon','Gorgon','Gorgon','8','Large','Magical Beast','Always neutral','8d10+40 (85 hp)',85,'+4','30 ft. (6 squares)','20 (–1 size, +11 natural), touch 9, flat-footed 20','+8/+17','Gore +12 melee (1d8+7)','10 ft./5 ft.','+11','+6','+5',21,10,21,2,12,9,'Listen +9, Spot +8','Alertness, Improved Initiative, Iron Will','{"special_attacks":"Breath weapon, trample 1d8+7","special_qualities":"Darkvision 60 ft., lowlight vision, scent"}'::jsonb,'A typical gorgon stands over 6 feet tall at the shoulder and measures 8 feet from snout to tail. It weighs about 4,000 pounds.

Gorgons are nothing if not aggressive. They attack intruders on sight, attempting to trample, gore, or petrify them. There is no way to calm these furious creatures, and they are impossible to domesticate.','{"full_attack":"Gore +12 melee (1d8+7)","statblock":{"hit_dice":"8d10+40 (85 hp)","hit_points":85,"base_attack_grapple":"+8/+17","attack":"Gore +12 melee (1d8+7)","full_attack":"Gore +12 melee (1d8+7)","space_reach":"10 ft./5 ft.","saves":"Fort +11, Ref +6, Will +5","abilities":{"str":"21","dex":"10","con":"21","int":"2","wis":"12","cha":"9"},"skills":"Listen +9, Spot +8","feats":"Alertness, Improved Initiative, Iron Will","special_attacks":"Breath weapon, trample 1d8+7","special_qualities":"Darkvision 60 ft., lowlight vision, scent"},"source_file":"monsters-g.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-g.html',true),
('gray_render','Gray Render','Gray Render','8','Large','Magical Beast','Usually neutral','10d10+70 (125 hp)',125,'+0','30 ft. (6 squares)','19 (–1 size, +10 natural), touch 9, flat-footed 19','+10/+20','Bite +15 melee (2d6+6)','10 ft./10 ft.','+14','+7','+4',23,10,24,3,12,8,'Hide +2, Spot +10, Survival +3','Cleave, Power Attack, Improved Bull Rush, Track','{"special_attacks":"Improved grab, rend 2d6+9","special_qualities":"Darkvision 60 ft., low-light vision, scent"}'::jsonb,'A gray render stands about 9 feet tall in spite of its hunched posture and is about 4 feet wide. It weighs about 4,000 pounds.

Gray renders are never found in groups. Each of these asexual creatures produces one offspring and carries it for a time in a pouch, but thereafter the young render must fend for itself.

A unique quality of the gray render is its tendency to bond with, protect, and provide for another creature (or group of creatures) native to its surroundings. Whether accepted or not, the render always attempts to remain fairly close, watching over its adopted charge(s) and daily bringing an offering of meat. It never willingly harms adopted creatures and retreats if they attack it.','{"full_attack":"Bite +15 melee (2d6+6); 2 claws +10 melee (1d6+3)","statblock":{"hit_dice":"10d10+70 (125 hp)","hit_points":125,"base_attack_grapple":"+10/+20","attack":"Bite +15 melee (2d6+6)","full_attack":"Bite +15 melee (2d6+6); 2 claws +10 melee (1d6+3)","space_reach":"10 ft./10 ft.","saves":"Fort +14, Ref +7, Will +4","abilities":{"str":"23","dex":"10","con":"24","int":"3","wis":"12","cha":"8"},"skills":"Hide +2, Spot +10, Survival +3","feats":"Cleave, Power Attack, Improved Bull Rush, Track","special_attacks":"Improved grab, rend 2d6+9","special_qualities":"Darkvision 60 ft., low-light vision, scent"},"source_file":"monsters-g.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-g.html',true),
